@startuml debugging_workflow
!theme plain
title Kernel Driver Debugging Workflow

participant Developer
participant Kernel as "Running Kernel"
participant Log as "dmesg/syslog"
participant Tracer as "ftrace/trace-cmd"
participant Debugger as "kgdb"

== Issue Detection ==
Developer -> Kernel: insmod my_driver.ko
Kernel -> Log: print probe messages
Developer -> Log: dmesg | tail
alt Error seen
  Developer -> Developer: Issue confirmed
else No error
  Developer -> Kernel: Trigger workload
  Kernel -> Log: may log on error
end

== Strategy: Add printk ==
Developer -> Developer: Add pr_info/pr_debug
Developer -> Kernel: Rebuild & reload
Kernel -> Log: Log output

Developer -> Developer: Check dmesg output
alt Issue located
  Developer -> Developer: Fix code
else Still confused
  Developer -> Tracer: Use dynamic debug
end

== Strategy: Dynamic Debug ==
Developer -> Tracer: Enable module debug
Tracer -> Kernel: echo "module my_driver +p"\n> /proc/dynamic_debug/control
Kernel -> Log: Verbose output
Developer -> Log: Check trace_pipe

Developer -> Developer: Issue clearer now?
alt Yes, fix code
else Need more detail
  Developer -> Tracer: Use ftrace
end

== Strategy: Function Trace ==
Developer -> Tracer: ftrace or trace-cmd
Developer -> Tracer: echo "my_probe" >\nset_ftrace_filter
Tracer -> Kernel: Monitor function calls
Tracer -> Tracer: Record call timings
Developer -> Tracer: trace-cmd report
Developer -> Developer: Analyze call graph

Developer -> Developer: Issue found?
alt Yes, fix code
else Timing issue
  Developer -> Debugger: Use kgdb
end

== Strategy: Remote Debugging ==
Developer -> Debugger: gdb vmlinux
Debugger -> Kernel: break my_probe
Kernel -> Debugger: Breakpoint hit
Debugger -> Developer: Single step code
Developer -> Debugger: Inspect variables
Developer -> Developer: Issue identified

== Verify Fix ==
Developer -> Kernel: Rebuild driver
Developer -> Kernel: Test fix
Kernel -> Log: No errors
Developer -> Developer: Issue resolved!

note right of Log
  dmesg - kernel message buffer
  /var/log/kern.log - syslog
  /proc/dynamic_debug/control
  /sys/kernel/debug/tracing/
end note

@enduml
